updated_utc: 2026-09-19T15:37:57Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-working-product-memory-2026-09-19.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-09-19.md

current_batch:
  date: 2026-09-19
  reports: 16
  manifest: docs/report-intake/2026-09-19/working-product-research/MANIFEST.md
  review: Every report has a disposition, corrections and concrete proof-of-use paths in report_decision_index and .uai/intake-outcome-ledger.uai.
  authority: Owner requirements and inspected current contracts first; research is advisory, never local execution or acceptance evidence.

applied_to_current_guidance:
  model_quality: R01/R05/R16; exact provenance and distinct weights, reference-first screens, behavioral invariants, untouched holdout and five decisive experiments.
  semantics_numerics: R02/R03/R04; tokenizer/template/state parity, five reference arms, teacher forcing, first-divergence traces, operation-specific tolerances and controlled quantization.
  browser_first_run: R08/R09; phase memory/timing budgets, worker ownership/cancellation, verified cache/default restoration and honest readiness states; preserve appearance.
  seed_transfer_storage: R10/R11/R12; authorized MiniModel initial seeds, capability discovery, bounded integrity/resume, all-member activation and retirement after verified replacement.
  data_experiments: R06/R07/R14; preserve frozen pilot, genuine independent review, masking/ablation readiness, stage taxonomy and compact reusable lessons.
  ownership_release: R13/R15; inspected owner per contract, immutable asset graph, actual promotion capabilities and external readback.

corrections:
  - Qwen3 diagnostic geometry is 28 layers, hidden 1024, MLP 3072, 16 Q heads, 8 KV heads and explicit head dimension 128; do not use the different Qwen dimensions in R02.
  - The 598308416-byte diagnostic is current row-wise Q8, not a Q4 estimate of a 1.1B model.
  - OPFS reads fill buffers; they do not automatically memory-map files into WASM. Ordinary WASM loads/stores permit unaligned accesses.
  - WebRTC data channels use SCTP over DTLS over UDP. No guessed Cicero/local IIS host, browser-version guarantee or paid cloud choice is established.
  - Six-member activation cannot publish a manifest before independent member renames; a service worker and two pointer writes do not prove atomic publication.
  - Source-framework load failure preceded converted-arm execution. Synthetic example results, candidate scores and placeholder revisions in reports are not measurements.
  - Existing Companion and browser client wiring must not be described as missing because August historical prose says so.

proposal_only:
  - GGUF/Candle, SLM3/Q4, Bao/BLAKE3, Min-P/template engine replacement, GPU/SIMD mandates, KV persistence, new training objectives/reallocation and object storage.
  - Numerical/quality/latency/RAM thresholds, model shortlist identities, licensing clearance and hosting capacity not independently measured or admitted.
  - Public report examples may support reviewed development cases; never label them secret holdout data.

current_status: Early alpha, never a working release; no qualified default, real numerical trace, useful acquired-model browser proof or live initial seed. No debt, obsolete code or legacy support before official owner acceptance.
historical_boundary: Earlier intake and closed experiments remain evidence only; see current decision index for history routing.
